    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12555" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ-οδύρομαι</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῡ</span>], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lament bitterly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τι πρὸς τὤγαλμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.141
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύχας</span> A <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pr.</u>
				637
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμαυτὴν καὶ γένος τὸ πᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					1122
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>
			<i>to</i> a person, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				1.9.8
			</span></i> (dub.): abs., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				606a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>take one's fill of lamentation</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπολοφύρομαι</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				1.463
			</span></i>.</div>
